% =======================================================
\section{Directional-Sea Stability Target}
\label{sec:sea3-stability-target}

The implementation is intended for oscillatory marine motion, not for an
arbitrary bounded specific-force sequence.  The quantitative source-word proof
of Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path} deliberately remains valid as
the stronger implementation-source envelope, but it can be much more
conservative than the physical deployment class because instantaneous source
bounds alone permit sample-to-sample combinations that no directional sea can
produce.  This section therefore states the stability result that the next
certificate generation is intended to discharge: stability of perturbations of
a physically admissible, oscillatory, multimodal directional sea family.

The result below is a \emph{conditional target theorem}.  Its composition
argument is complete once the listed SEA0/P1--P5 certificates are available,
but this manuscript does not claim that the new SEA0 directional-sea enclosure,
the SEA3 P3/P4 margins, or the 45-degree SEA3 P5 capture certificate have
already been constructed.

\subsection{Three-partition directional sea class}

Fix
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{M_{\max}=3.}
 \label{eq:sea3-mmax}
\end{equation}
For partition $r\in\{1,2,3\}$ let
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_r=(H_r,T_{p,r},\gamma_r,\beta_r,s_r)
 \label{eq:sea3-partition-parameter}
\end{equation}
collect significant-height contribution, peak period, JONSWAP peak-enhancement
factor, mean propagation direction, and directional-spreading parameter.  An
inactive slot is represented by $H_r=0$ rather than by a change of model
dimension.  Under the spectral convention used here, $\gamma_r=1$ gives the
PM limit of the JONSWAP frequency family.

The directional elevation spectrum is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 E(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 =
 \sum_{r=1}^{3}
 S_J(\omega;H_r,T_{p,r},\gamma_r)
 D_r(\vartheta;\beta_r,s_r,\omega),
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}
\end{equation}
where each $D_r$ is nonnegative and normalized over direction.  The partition
energies are coupled by
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{H_s^2=\sum_{r=1}^{3}H_r^2.}
 \label{eq:sea3-total-energy}
\end{equation}
Thus a one-system sea, wind sea plus swell, crossing swell, and a
three-component multimodal sea all belong to one fixed-dimensional parameter
family.  In particular, the proof is not allowed to maximize all three $H_r$
independently while also holding $H_s$ fixed.

The sea parameters evolve through a compact transition relation
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_{k+1}\in\mathcal R_\lambda(\lambda_k),
 \label{eq:sea3-rate-relation}
\end{equation}
whose component bounds include physically justified limits on changes of
$H_r$, $T_{p,r}$, $\gamma_r$, $\beta_r$, and $s_r$.  Those rate limits are
theorem assumptions to be certified by SEA0; they are not fitted to the eight
reference simulations.

\subsection{Directional response and oscillatory source}

The spectrum of Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum} is not converted to
independent Cartesian acceleration boxes.  Let
$G_{\rm imu}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)$ denote the certified directional
sea-to-CoG/IMU response family.  The corresponding matrix-valued source
spectrum is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Phi_u(\omega;\lambda)
 =
 \int
 G_{\rm imu}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 E(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)
 G_{\rm imu}^{*}(\omega,\vartheta;\lambda)\,d\vartheta .
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-matrix-spectrum}
\end{equation}
It retains the physically coupled cross spectra between the measured vector
components.

For deterministic certification SEA0 supplies an outward enclosure of this
family by an oscillator/shaping state or an equivalent hard finite-window
dynamic constraint,
\begin{align}
 x^s_{k+1}&=A_s(\lambda_k)x^s_k+B_s(\lambda_k)w_k, \nonumber\\
 u^s_k&=C_s(\lambda_k)x^s_k,
 \label{eq:sea3-shaping-system}
\end{align}
with the oscillatory blocks preserving phase continuity.  For an individual
undamped oscillator, for example,
\begin{equation}
 \begin{bmatrix}q_{c,k+1}\\q_{s,k+1}\end{bmatrix}
 =
 \begin{bmatrix}
 \cos\omega h&-\sin\omega h\\
 \sin\omega h& \cos\omega h
 \end{bmatrix}
 \begin{bmatrix}q_{c,k}\\q_{s,k}\end{bmatrix}.
 \label{eq:sea3-oscillator-step}
\end{equation}
The actual theorem input is separated as
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{u_k=u^s_k+d^s_k,}
 \label{eq:sea3-perturbed-source}
\end{equation}
where motion generated by admissible changes of the three sea partitions is
part of $u^s$, while $d^s$ denotes bounded out-of-class/model-mismatch input.
The deterministic theorem uses a hard finite-window bound on this input.  A
probabilistic statement for random sea realizations is a later corollary; no
infinite-time pointwise bound is inferred merely from a Gaussian spectrum.

\subsection{Exact tuner reachability and source-language refinement}

The deployed measurement-only adaptation path remains inside the source:
\begin{equation}
 u_k
 \longrightarrow
 \text{WavePeriodEstimator/prior source}
 \longrightarrow
 \text{band variance/EMAs}
 \longrightarrow
 (\tau_k,\sigma_{aw,k},R_{S,k},T_{S,k}),
 \label{eq:sea3-tuner-chain}
\end{equation}
including the exact stage/commit and pseudo-update scheduler state.  Before the
WavePeriodEstimator has produced a finite positive frequency, shipping code
uses the fixed $0.2$ Hz tuning prior.  The tuner update for sample $k$ executes
before the current sample advances the WavePeriodEstimator, so a newly finite
period estimate can affect the tuner no earlier than the following valid
sample.  Takeover uses the first finite positive estimator value and does
\emph{not} wait for \texttt{WavePeriodEstimator::isReady()}.  Conversely,
filter \texttt{TunerReady} is based on the SeaStateAutoTuner's own readiness and
may therefore occur while the fixed-prior branch is still active.  SEA3/P2 must
retain these as distinct source modes rather than treating Live entry as proof
that the sea-period statistic has settled.

Denote the tuner memory by $z^t_k$ and scheduler/hybrid source memory by $q_k$.
The augmented exogenous state is therefore
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\zeta_k=(x^s_k,\lambda_k,z^t_k,q_k).}
 \label{eq:sea3-augmented-source}
\end{equation}
The SEA3 certificate must establish the sound language inclusions
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal L_{\rm actual\ sea}
 \subseteq
 \widehat{\mathcal L}_{\rm SEA3}
 \subseteq
 \mathcal L_{\rm current\ source}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-language-inclusions}
\end{equation}
The right-hand language is the existing correlated implementation-source
language; its frozen P2 semantics are not redefined.  Replay records may
falsify either inclusion but may not be used to construct the SEA3 language.

\subsection{Finite sea windows}

With two or three active partitions the modal frequencies need not be
commensurate, so no common wave period is assumed.  Let $T_W$ be a finite
\emph{sea window} and
\begin{equation}
 N_W=\left\lceil T_W/h\right\rceil
 \label{eq:sea3-window-samples}
\end{equation}
its sample count.  SEA0/P3 must choose $T_W$ from a certified
finite-window information condition, not from a replayed trajectory.  A
representative target is
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{\mathcal O_{k,N_W}\succeq\alpha_O I,\qquad \alpha_O>0}
 \label{eq:sea3-window-information}
\end{equation}
for every admissible SEA3 window in each fixed-dimensional Live mode.

Let $M(\zeta)\succ0$ be the source-indexed information metric and write
\begin{equation}
 V(e,\zeta)=e^\top M(\zeta)e
 \label{eq:sea3-lifted-energy}
\end{equation}
in local error coordinates, with the exact Cayley lift of
Sec.~\ref{sec:stability-widening-source-path} used for finite attitude error.
The key nonlinear certificate is the window-wise inequality
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k+N_W}
 \le
 \rho V_k
 +\gamma_sD_{s,k}
 +\gamma_nD_{n,k},
 \qquad 0<\rho<1,
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-window-dissipation}
\end{equation}
where $D_{s,k}$ and $D_{n,k}$ are hard finite-window energies of model mismatch
and measurement/process perturbations.  No one-sample decrease of $V$ is
required; growth inside an oscillation is allowed.

\subsection{Main conditional stability theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Three-mode directional-sea regional practical stability and
finite capture]
\label{thm:sea3-regional-practical-stability}
Assume the following hold for both fixed-dimensional Normal-Live modes.

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*),leftmargin=2.1em]
\item SEA0 supplies a sound outward enclosure of the three-partition
directional sea class of Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-directional-spectrum}--
\eqref{eq:sea3-shaping-system}, its declared rate-bounded parameter evolution,
and its directional vessel/IMU response.
\item P1 places the execution in the declared Normal-Live operating branch,
including the current no-accelerometer-rejection condition and the declared
startup prior/estimator source split.
\item P2 proves Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-language-inclusions} while preserving the
exact deployed period-source mode, tuner, parameter-EMA, stage/commit, and
pseudo-update scheduler history.
\item P3 supplies bounded positive source metrics and a strict finite-window
linear information/contraction margin on every SEA3-complete window.
\item P4 verifies Eq.~\eqref{eq:sea3-window-dissipation} for the exact nonlinear
shipping word map on an invariant inner funnel
$\mathcal F_{\rm inner}$, with every prefix inside its declared chart/source
domain.
\item P5 proves that every admitted 45-degree entrance state reaches
$\mathcal F_{\rm inner}$ in at most $K_{\rm cap}$ samples while respecting the
hybrid obligations.
\end{enumerate}

Then for the capture time $k_c$ and every integer $m\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k_c+mN_W}
 \le
 \rho^mV_{k_c}
 +
 \sum_{j=0}^{m-1}
 \rho^{m-1-j}
 \left(\gamma_sD_{s,j}+\gamma_nD_{n,j}\right).
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-iss-sum}
\end{equation}
If $D_{s,j}\le\overline D_s$ and
$D_{n,j}\le\overline D_n$, then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \limsup_{m\to\infty}V_{k_c+mN_W}
 \le
 \frac{\gamma_s\overline D_s+\gamma_n\overline D_n}{1-\rho}.
 }
 \label{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate}
\end{equation}
Consequently, uniform metric lower and prefix bounds give a regional practical
ISS bound on the full error between window endpoints.  When both perturbation
energies vanish, the inner error converges exponentially in lifted sea windows.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
P5 gives a finite $k_c$ with the state in the P4 invariant funnel.
Equation~\eqref{eq:sea3-window-dissipation} can then be iterated on consecutive
SEA3-complete windows because P2/SEA0 preserve source completeness and P4
preserves the funnel.  Summing the resulting geometric series gives
Eqs.~\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-iss-sum} and
\eqref{eq:sea3-practical-ultimate}.  The P3/P4 uniform metric and prefix bounds
convert endpoint energy to an error norm at all intermediate samples.
\end{proof}

The theorem is called \emph{regional} because the present entrance set is
fixed at 45 degrees.  A semiglobal corollary would require the certificate
construction to succeed for every prescribed compact entrance subset of the
Cayley chart; that stronger claim is not assumed here.

\subsection{Shipping envelope used by the new certificate}

The SEA3 construction must use the current deployed clamps rather than the
historical wider proof envelope.  The source at this revision gives
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{@{}ll@{}}
\toprule
Quantity & Current bound\\
\midrule
tuning frequency & $0.03\le f_{\rm tune}\le1.2$ Hz\\
OU time constant & $0.02\le\tau\le12$ s\\
OU acceleration standard deviation & $\sigma_{aw}\le4$ m/s$^2$\\
$R_S$ scalar clamp & $0.15\le R_S\le100$\\
$S=0$ pseudo-update period & $0.005\le T_S\le0.150$ s\\
dynamic EMA horizon & $\le35$ s\\
Normal-Live accelerometer rejection & not admitted\\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
These are source-parity values, not fitted sea parameters.

\subsection{Retained SEA0 subcertificates and temporal structure}

Two replay-free, non-promoting SEA0 subcertificates are retained at this
revision.  The spectral-moment bridge fixes the PM anchor and multimodal moment
composition, and records why a response-weighted finite band is required before
acceleration moments are finite.  Its current padded JONSWAP shape screen over
$1\le\gamma\le7$ gives
\begin{equation}
 0.709119591169\le T_{z,\eta}/T_p\le0.829083684991,
\end{equation}
but this numerical continuum screen is not yet an interval-integration
promotion and may not prune P2.

The WavePeriodEstimator front-end subcertificate validates the implemented
steady sinusoidal transfer over the committed 5 ms, 0.03--1.2 Hz channel.  Its
period distortion is below about 59 ppm, so discrete front-end warping is not
the current limiter.  More importantly for startup, the source default
high-pass/leak corner is 0.02 Hz, hence the estimator cannot accept moment
statistics before
\begin{equation}
 t_{\rm settle}=\frac{6}{2\pi(0.02)}\approx47.75\ {\rm s}.
\end{equation}
This is only a lower bound on the first possible finite period: a valid moment
ratio can appear later.  The shipping outer wrapper uses a 10 s online-tuner
warmup and the tuner itself has its own frequency/variance readiness, so
\texttt{TunerReady} and even Live handoff can precede this period-estimator
settling bound.  The SEA3 source language must therefore preserve the fixed
0.2 Hz prior branch, estimator-driven branch, and their one-sample causal
takeover edge.

The tightened 150 ms pseudo-update ceiling still gives a maximum nominal
30-sample $S=0$ recurrence, now certified by the retained scheduler primitive.
No separate sizing helper or diagnostic workflow is required for these facts;
they are consumed by the canonical \texttt{ou3-proof.yml} route.

The remaining SEA0 promotion obligation is the directional vessel/IMU response
and finite-band multimodal moment enclosure, followed by finite moment/log-period
dynamics after estimator takeover and the sound SEA3-to-P2 language inclusion.
Those steps are intentionally left for the next proof increment rather than
adding another fallback proof route here.
